{
  "module": "Training: how the numbers are learned",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "teacher-forcing",
    "title": "Teacher forcing: training on all positions at once",
    "summary": "How training uses one forward pass to get a prediction, and a loss, at every position of a text: the shifted targets, feeding the true tokens, and why this is not how the model generates.",
    "covers": ["teacher-forcing"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "next-token-loss",
        "reason": "Teacher forcing is how the next-token loss is computed for a whole text at once."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "generation-loop",
        "reason": "It is defined in contrast with generating one token at a time."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "training-basics",
        "reason": "It is a trick used only in training, so training and inference must already be clear."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "slow-way",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "When the model "
            },
            {
              "text": "generates",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", it works one token at a time: a full pass to produce one token, then another pass for the next."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "If training worked the same way, learning from a text of 1,000 tokens would take 1,000 separate passes. That would be very slow, and there is a better way."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 20, 73)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "shifted-targets",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "In training we already have the whole text. So the "
            },
            {
              "text": "targets",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " are simply the same text "
            },
            {
              "text": "shifted by one position",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "For the text "
            },
            {
              "text": "The cat sat on the mat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ":"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "input: The, cat, sat, on, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "target: cat, sat, on, the, mat"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "At the position of "
            },
            {
              "text": "The",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " the right answer is "
            },
            {
              "text": "cat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". At "
            },
            {
              "text": "cat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " it is "
            },
            {
              "text": "sat",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and so on."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 73)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "true-tokens",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Notice what the input contains: the "
            },
            {
              "text": "true",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " tokens from the text, not tokens the model itself guessed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Feeding the true tokens as input, instead of the model's own guesses, is called "
            },
            {
              "text": "teacher forcing",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Even if the model would have guessed badly at one position, the next position still gets the true text."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 73)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "one-pass",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Because every input token is already known, one forward pass gives predictions at "
            },
            {
              "text": "all n positions at once",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". You saw that the model produces a next-token distribution at every position."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Each position's prediction is compared with its target, the loss is averaged over all positions, and that one loss is backpropagated through the whole network."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So a 1,000-token text costs one pass, not 1,000."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 73)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "no-peeking",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "There is an obvious worry: the target for position "
            },
            {
              "text": "t",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is the token at "
            },
            {
              "text": "t + 1",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and that token is in the input. Could position "
            },
            {
              "text": "t",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " just look at it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "It cannot. Position t is never allowed to see its own target. The mechanism that guarantees this is called the causal mask, covered in the attention module."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 73)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "only-training",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Teacher forcing is a "
            },
            {
              "text": "training",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " technique. When the model generates, there is no true text to feed in. It has to use its own earlier outputs, one token at a time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "So the same model is used in two ways: all positions at once with the true tokens in training, and one token at a time with its own tokens in generation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 20, 73)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
